  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY NIGHT THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 1242 PM CDT Thu Aug 13 2026\n\nFlow aloft stays mostly zonal to slightly northwesterly through\nthe period. A more trackable shortwave works towards the area\nfor the weekend. This tries to nudge cold front through slowly \nthrough the weekend. This should eventually work to limit the\noppressive heat, at least for a bit. Showers and storms chances\ncontinue both Saturday and Sunday before looking to start to\ndecrease early next week.\n\nMid and upper level ridging works back in from the west by\nTuesday into Wednesday that in the current deterministic\nsynoptic picture looks to put the area back into hot and humid\nconditions with thunderstorms developing near or just north of\nthe area, somewhat similarly to the current pattern.",
